# M5 appliance readiness gate (ARCHITECTURE.md §9): "The service remains
# disabled until preflight confirms a display, input device, writable
# state directory, USB access, and at least one audio output." This
# oneshot unit runs `aa-headunit-diagnostics preflight` (the same command
# an operator can run by hand) and, via `aa-headunit-kiosk@.service`'s own
# `Requires=`/`After=` on this unit, gates whether the kiosk session is
# even attempted each boot — a non-zero exit here (a real, distinct
# `PreflightFailed` error, not just an unsupported board) stops the kiosk
# unit from starting instead of letting it fail messily against
# incomplete hardware.
#
# Runs as the dedicated `aa-headunit` user (not root) so the
# `preflight_state_dir` check confirms the *actual* runtime user can
# write to /var/lib/aa-headunit, not just that root can.
#
# NOT YET real-hardware-tested as a systemd unit (only the underlying
# `aa-headunit-diagnostics preflight` command has been run directly and
# confirmed passing) — this project's own operator has deliberately not
# enabled/started it yet. See `aa-headunit-kiosk@.service`'s own doc
# comment for the larger reason (a genuine reboot risk this session
# chose to defer).

[Unit]
Description=Android Auto head unit appliance readiness check
Documentation=https://github.com/blakereuben/pi-auto-headunit

[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=aa-headunit
Group=aa-headunit
ExecStart=/usr/bin/aa-headunit-diagnostics preflight
